  "_linkedCounterDisplayNote": "resolveLinkedCounterDisplay (placementParams.ts, slice 2c) <-> Swift PlacementParams.resolveLinkedCounterDisplay: what a LINKED counting square/row shows — a thin wrapper over resolveSquareState. `window` given (the placing board's {startDate,endDate}) = the ROOT's increment sum inside THAT window, whatever the row's own stamp; no window + window-stamped row = its own stamp; no window + any other linked row = contextlessCounterState (the root's lifetime sum). `sealedAt` bounds every event first (boundWindowContextAtSeal). Optional `placement` {targetOverride,targetKind,childTargets,titleOverride} applies the square's parameters. No event map = no events (0, incomplete). currentCount − baseline and the latch are never read. Consumed by packages/shared/tests/algorithms/taskEvents.test.ts and apps/ios/OYBCTests/TaskEventVectorTests.swift.",
